extend ../layout.pug

block content
  h2=  t('emails.transactionLinkRedeemed.title', { senderAlias })
  .text-block
    include ../includes/salutation.pug
    //- One paragraph is one piece of news, and ONE sentence of the catalogue says it: for
    //- somebody who opened their account with this link the sentence itself says so. Two
    //- whole keys, chosen inside the expression -- nothing is joined on here. A half-sentence
    //- glued behind the first one left a full stop before its dash ("… eingelöst. — und ist
    //- neu bei Gradido."), and every language wants the arrival in a place of its own.
    p= t(newMember ? 'emails.transactionLinkRedeemed.hasAcceptedYourThanksNewMember' : 'emails.transactionLinkRedeemed.hasAcceptedYourThanks', { senderAlias, senderCommunity })
  .content
    h2= t('emails.general.transactionDetails')
    div(class="p_content")= t('emails.general.amountGDD', { amountGDD: transactionAmount })
      br
      +humanText(t('emails.transactionLinkRedeemed.memo', { transactionMemo }))
      br
      = t('emails.general.detailsYouFindOnLinkToYourAccount')

    //- The way to the person who accepted: their conversation, where the booking stands --
        with the greeting's picture, where the link was a greeting. Green and inside the card,
        as every button that leads to a person (webflow.css), above the gold way into the
        account. The contact page opens the window with the member `with` names, of the
        community `community` names -- the address the reply button of the transfer mail has.
        Without the two uuids there is no such way, and the button is left out.

        On a line of its own, centred as everything in the card is. Its lower margin is taken
        off, so that the two buttons stand 25px apart and not 50.

        Each of the two is written as ONE value of the address (encodeURIComponent). Across the
        border the member's id is what the other server answered with; an "&" or a "#" in it
        would otherwise end the value and begin something of its own. A uuid stays as it is.
    if senderCommunityUuid && senderUuid
      div
        a.button-5(href=`${communityURL}/contacts?with=${encodeURIComponent(senderUuid)}&community=${encodeURIComponent(senderCommunityUuid)}` style="margin: 25px 0 0 0")
          include ../includes/chatbox-icon.pug
          span #{t('emails.general.toConversation')}

    a.button-3(href=`${communityURL}/transactions`) #{t('emails.general.toAccount')}

    include ../includes/doNotReply.pug
